{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"DHI-hxqh-pxmh-yxim-6c64","published":"2026-11-11T16:44:09Z","modified":"2026-11-20T00:00:09.473051479Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-116272"],"summary":"MIME::Field::ParamVal versions before 5.521 for Perl do not flag a duplicate boundary parameter whose name contains a…","details":"MIME::Field::ParamVal versions before 5.521 for Perl do not flag a duplicate boundary parameter whose name contains a nested comment.\n\nA parameter written boundary((c))=\"A\" or boundary(\\))=\"A\" is stored under that literal name rather than as boundary. A second boundary parameter is then not reported as a duplicate, and MIME::Parser splits the message on it.\n\nReaders that skip comments as RFC 5322 allows take the first boundary instead. A remote sender can hide an attachment from a filter that relies on ambiguous_content() while the recipient's mail client shows it.","affected":[{"package":{"name":"perl-mime-tools","ecosystem":"Docker Hardened Images:Alpine:3.24","purl":"pkg:apk/dhi/perl-mime-tools"},"versions":["5.517-r0","5.517-r1"],"database_specific":{"owner_kind":"HSP","source":"https://github.com/docker-hardened-images/advisories/blob/main/dhi/osv/2026/DHI-hxqh-pxmh-yxim-6c64.json"}}],"references":[{"type":"ADVISORY","url":"https://scout.docker.com/v/DHI-hxqh-pxmh-yxim-6c64"},{"type":"ADVISORY","url":"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-116272"},{"type":"ADVISORY","url":"https://security.alpinelinux.org/vuln/CVE-2026-116272"},{"type":"ADVISORY","url":"https://alas.aws.amazon.com/AL2023/ALAS-2026-3425.html"},{"type":"ADVISORY","url":"http://cve.mitre.org/cgi-bin/cvename.cgi?name=CVE-2026-116273"},{"type":"ADVISORY","url":"http://cve.mitre.org/cgi-bin/cvename.cgi?name=CVE-2026-116272"},{"type":"ADVISORY","url":"http://cve.mitre.org/cgi-bin/cvename.cgi?name=CVE-2026-116271"},{"type":"ADVISORY","url":"http://cve.mitre.org/cgi-bin/cvename.cgi?name=CVE-2026-116270"},{"type":"ADVISORY","url":"http://cve.mitre.org/cgi-bin/cvename.cgi?name=CVE-2026-116269"},{"type":"ADVISORY","url":"http://cve.mitre.org/cgi-bin/cvename.cgi?name=CVE-2026-116268"},{"type":"ADVISORY","url":"http://cve.mitre.org/cgi-bin/cvename.cgi?name=CVE-2026-116267"},{"type":"ADVISORY","url":"http://cve.mitre.org/cgi-bin/cvename.cgi?name=CVE-2026-116265"},{"type":"ADVISORY","url":"http://cve.mitre.org/cgi-bin/cvename.cgi?name=CVE-2026-116264"},{"type":"ADVISORY","url":"https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-116272"},{"type":"ADVISORY","url":"https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-116272"},{"type":"ADVISORY","url":"http://people.ubuntu.com/~ubuntu-security/cve/CVE-2026-116272"}],"severity":[{"type":"CVSS_V3","score":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:L/A:N"}]}